# Project Context

Read `AGENTS.md` first. It is the canonical project-wide guidance.

## Repository intelligence folders

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `.github/instructions/` | Scoped coding rules (`*.instructions.md`) — loaded automatically via matching `.cursor/rules/` |
| `.github/agents/` | Reviewer personas (`*.agent.md`) for focused reviews |
| `.github/prompts/` | Task templates (`*.prompt.md`) for repeatable workflows |
| `.github/skills/` | GitHub Copilot skills mirror — keep in sync with `.agents/skills/` |
| `.agents/skills/` | Cursor project skills — read the relevant `SKILL.md` before specialized work |
| `docs/adr/` | Architecture decision records |
| `docs/context/` | Phase history, lessons learned, reference patterns |
| `docs/deployment/` | Railway, Salesforce, and onboarding runbooks |
| `docs/testing/` | Proof docs, UAT scripts, eval notes |
| `docs/orchestrator/` | LangGraph case triage orchestrator design; **`new-node-phase-completion-checklist.md`** for any new node |
| `docs/agents/` | Agent capability and findings docs |

## Workflow

1. Read `AGENTS.md` for global rules.
2. For scoped edits, follow the matching `.github/instructions/*.instructions.md` (also attached via file-scoped Cursor rules).
3. For specialized tasks, read the matching `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md` or `.github/prompts/*.prompt.md`.
4. For architecture or phase context, check `docs/adr/` and `docs/context/project-memory.md`.
5. When adding an orchestrator node, follow `docs/orchestrator/new-node-phase-completion-checklist.md` (Final Verdict + UI + smoke).
6. For reviews, adopt the persona from the matching `.github/agents/*.agent.md`.

Do not duplicate Salesforce, NestJS, RAG, Open WebUI, React chat, security, or release rules into Cursor files. Keep the source of truth in `AGENTS.md`, `.github/instructions/`, and `docs/adr/`.

Use CodeTrellis when available: MCP server `.vscode/mcp.json`, matrix `.codetrellis/cache/AgentForce/matrix.prompt`.
